			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2787336">
									

<p><strong>December 2018 edit:</strong> I wrote this during a miserable time in my life and it shows here. Trans people can and do have happy endings, and they can and do even in the Foundation's setting. I know this now that my life has improved but I also know better than to edit or delete this work. It is what it is. -1.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;old&nbsp;author&nbsp;post</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><em>Unless otherwise stated, any graphics or images in my articles are made and/or taken by me.</em></p>
<p>Unforeseen technical note: This page was BLANK for no discernible reason until Cimmerian somehow fixed the source code<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-141415-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-141415-1')">1</a></sup> and got Wikidot to realize that HTML is still a thing even when one [[=]] is mistyped. Thank you Cimm!</p>
<hr />
<p>Now then, original intended author post:</p>
<p>Coldpost. I'm&#8230; not really sure what this is. It appears to be me channeling the emotion and pain behind some damaging events in my life into a fictional setting and scenario as a coping mechanism. Art imitates life and all that. Whatever it is, I don't really care, it's up now and we'll see what happens with it.</p>
</div>
